Package: zmctp
Type: Package
Title: Zero-Modified Complex 'Tri-Parametric' Pearson Distribution for
        Overdispersed Count Data
Version: 0.1.4
Authors@R: c(
    person("Rasheedat", "Oladoja",
           email = "roladoja@ttu.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-5883-8039"))
    , person("Kabir Opeyemi", "Olorede",
             role = "aut",
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5065-6516"))
    )
Description: Provides probability, distribution, quantile and random-generation
    functions for the complex three-parameter Pearson distribution and its
    zero-inflated extension. Maximum likelihood fitting uses analytic profiling
    of the mixing probability, multiple starting points and numerical boundary
    diagnostics. The parent family is described in the 2003 study
    <doi:10.1007/s00362-002-0134-7>.
